@page "/"

<PageTitle>cv-maker</PageTitle>

<h1>A CV tailored to the job, without the LaTeX</h1>

<p class="lede">
    Enter your history once. Paste a job posting. Pick a template. Get a typeset PDF.
</p>

<section class="cards">
    <article>
        <h2>1. Your facts</h2>
        @* Was "or paste your LinkedIn page and let it be extracted". There is no extraction:
           no endpoint accepts a LinkedIn page or an uploaded CV, and the profile-extractor
           agent is not reachable from any route. Advertising it set every new visitor up to
           look for a feature that does not exist. *@
        <p>Type your history in, one fact per achievement. It stays editable.</p>
        <NavLink class="button" href="profile">Build your profile</NavLink>
    </article>
    <article>
        <h2>2. The posting</h2>
        <p>Paste the advert. It is read to work out what the employer screens for — never to invent experience you do not have.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
        <h2>3. The PDF</h2>
        <p>Typeset properly, in the template you pick. There is an ATS-safe layout for the systems that mangle two-column CVs.</p>
        <NavLink class="button" href="generate">Generate</NavLink>
    </article>
</section>
